                  <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_608">York, Yorkshire. Benedictine
                        abbey of Saint Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>A detached portion from the end
                        of Oxford, Corpus Christi College, MS 193: see the agreement of the contents
                        of Corpus and Tiberius with no. 56 of Henry Savile's MSS.</p><p>Leland saw
                        at York ten works of Rolle, nine of which occur in the same order in the
                        Corpus MS, whilst the tenth is in Tiberius (B121.7–15).</p><p>The Cotton
                        leaves have been damaged by fire. Written area about the same as in the
                        Corpus MS, allowing for shrinkage due to fire. 46 long
                     lines.</p></provenance>
